{"name":"Fly Away","hex":"#85b3f3","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"fly-away","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Alternative form of flyaway."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fly-away"}],"entries":[{"title":"Fly Away (Banaroo album)","blocks":[{"text":"Fly Away is the fourth studio album by the German group Banaroo. It's also the final album recorded with original Banaroo members Bobby, Steffy, Vito, and Cat, before the group disbanded in 2008."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/4/47/Banaroo_-_Fly_Away.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fly_Away_(Banaroo_album)"},{"title":"Fly Away (Corrinne May album)","blocks":[{"text":"Fly Away is the first album by Corrinne May, released in 2001 by Corrmay Gourmet Music. It was subsequently released by Yellow Music (M&M) in Singapore, released by the Major Chord label in Japan and by Forward Music in Taiwan and Hong Kong in 2005. The album was subsequently re-released by Playmusic and Warner Music in Singapore."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/a/a6/Corrinne_May_Fly_Away.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fly_Away_(Corrinne_May_album)"},{"title":"Fly Away (Lenny Kravitz song)","blocks":[{"text":"\"Fly Away\" is a song by American singer Lenny Kravitz. It was released as the fourth single from his fifth studio album, 5 (1998). Released to radio on May 11, 1998, \"Fly Away\" peaked at number 12 on the US Billboard Hot 100, topped the charts of Iceland and the United Kingdom, and peaked within the top 10 of the charts of several other countries, including Australia, Canada, Ireland, and New Zealand. The song won a Grammy Award for Best Male Rock Performance in 1999."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/5/59/Lenny_Fly_Away.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fly_Away_(Lenny_Kravitz_song)"},{"title":"Fly","blocks":[{"text":"A fly is an insect of the order Diptera, named for the single pair of wings. The hindwings have evolved into halteres, organs that sense rotation, giving flies precise control of their flight. Diptera is a large order containing more than 150,000 species, including horse-flies, crane flies, hoverflies, mosquitoes and others."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ea/Bessenbandzweefvlieg_Vrouwtje_%282%29.JPG/330px-Bessenbandzweefvlieg_Vrouwtje_%282%29.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fly"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bb/Anthomyiidae_%28female%29_%2810144905255%29.jpg/500px-Anthomyiidae_%28female%29_%2810144905255%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bb/Anthomyiidae_%28female%29_%2810144905255%29.jpg/1280px-Anthomyiidae_%28female%29_%2810144905255%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bb/Anthomyiidae_%28female%29_%2810144905255%29.jpg/500px-Anthomyiidae_%28female%29_%2810144905255%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"An Anthomyiid species showing characteristic dipteran features: large eyes, small antennae, sucking mouthparts, single pair of flying wings, hindwings reduced to clublike halteres","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AAnthomyiidae_(female)_(10144905255).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9a/RHYACOPHILA_DORSALIS_Male_Pont_Forge_de_Sailly_Watigny_02_MHNT.jpg/500px-RHYACOPHILA_DORSALIS_Male_Pont_Forge_de_Sailly_Watigny_02_MHNT.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=p